      "title": "One policy can contain coverage on different people",
      "narration": "Marcus has a two hundred fifty thousand dollar base policy on his own life. He wants to understand available protection for Elena and their children. A rider can add coverage on another eligible person without making that person the base insured. Keep a simple map: Marcus is insured under the base policy, Elena might be insured under an other-insured term rider, and eligible children might have a children's term rider. Ownership and beneficiary designations remain separate questions. Being named as a beneficiary does not itself insure that person's life. Read the person and benefit identified in each part of the issued contract.",
