      "title": "A spouse rider pays for the spouse’s covered death",
      "narration": "Suppose Marcus's policy includes a fifty thousand dollar term rider on Elena. If Elena dies from a covered cause while that rider is in force, the stated rider benefit is fifty thousand dollars. Marcus is still living, so his two hundred fifty thousand dollar base death benefit is not triggered by her death. An other-insured rider may cover a spouse or another eligible person under the contract; the product's name and eligibility rules matter. The additional coverage can have its own term, cost and conversion conditions. Do not assume it is permanent just because the base policy is whole life.",
