      "title": "Family coverage is a structure, not one universal benefit",
      "narration": "A family term arrangement combines the relevant term coverage for a spouse and children with the base insured's policy, depending on the product design. Some insurers use separate riders instead of one form called a family rider. The important exam task is to match each life to its benefit. This is different from a joint first-death policy paying once when the first of two insured people dies, and different from survivorship insurance paying at the second death. A household label does not tell you the claim trigger. Use the schedule of insured people, amounts and terms rather than adding every amount into one imagined family death benefit.",
